═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ THEORETICAL-NOTES ← §§ T24-depth-hints
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  LSP-library choices :
    tower-lsp : tokio + trait-based • most popular • recommend
    lsp-server : crossbeam + lower-level • rust-analyzer-lineage
    async-lsp : tower-middleware • newer • flexible
    recommend tower-lsp ∵ maturity + docs + community
  Sync-models :
    full-reparse : simple + <300ms on-small-files
    incremental-AST : complex + gold-standard for-large-files
    recommend full-reparse ∵ our-parser 1.8M-tok/s • likely-fast-enough
    upgrade to-incremental if-profiling-shows-need
  Subprocess-driver design :
    per-request spawn : simple • high-overhead
    long-lived daemon : complex • fast
    recommend hybrid : spawn-per-request w/ warm-pool
    parser.exe cold-start measured → tune from there
  Hover-content :
    markdown strongly-preferred ← LSP 3.17 native
    code-blocks w/ language-tag → syntax-highlight rendered
    tables for type-info (inferred-at + effect-row + refinements)
  Completion-ranking :
    prefix-match first • then-fuzzy • then-semantic-similarity
    insert-text-format : snippet for patterns • plaintext for glyphs
    documentation : markdown with specs-ref-link
  Workspace-index :
    SQLite : simple + fast + file-backed-persistence
    in-memory HashMap : faster but no-persistence
    recommend SQLite ∵ workspace-index survives-restart

